{number: 145}
{title: There is Sunshine}
{key: Ab}

{start_of_verse: 1}
There is [Ab] sunshine in my soul today,
More [Db] glorious and [Ab] bright
Than glows in any earthly sky,
For [Eb7] Jesus is my [Ab] light.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
O there's [Db] sunshine, blessed [Ab] sunshine,
When the [Fm] peaceful, happy moments [Eb7] roll;
When [Ab] Jesus shows His smiling face,
There is [Db] sunshine [Eb7] in the [Ab] soul.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
There is [Ab] music in my soul today,
A [Db] carol to my [Ab] King,
And Jesus, listening, can hear
The [Eb7] song I cannot [Ab] sing.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
There is [Ab] gladness in my soul today,
And [Db] hope and praise and [Ab] love,
For blessings which He gives me now,
For [Eb7] joys laid up a-[Ab] bove.
{end_of_verse}
